#==============================================================================================
#
#   code - The Code node: per-element Base snippets over a geometry set
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       A Code node runs the user's snippet once per point, vertex, primitive, number or
#       once for the detail (Houdini's Attribute Wrangle). luce-kernel checks the snippet
#       with the Base compiler's checker, lowers it to a column program and runs it over
#       chunks of elements on every core; this module says what the snippet's API means
#       for a mesh (`stubs.lucb` is the API the snippet is checked against, `bindings.lucb`
#       what each member reads and writes), binds the mesh's columns, and builds the
#       output set from the columns the program wrote.
#
#       Positions: geocore keeps f32 positions relative to an f64 origin. A snippet sees
#       world positions as f32 (`P = position + origin`, rounded once); written positions
#       go back as `(f32)((f64)P - origin)`. With the usual zero origin both are exact and
#       the position column is read in place.
#
#==============================================================================================
